From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:08:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the hashed sort's assert-only helper only when asserts are on

Assert-only code in hashed_sort.cpp binds values that only D_ASSERT()
reads, so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the
bindings are unused and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable
say so. The assert-only lines are compiled only when assertions are
enabled, with the side-effecting call kept in both builds, which is the
shape upstream gives the file later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp
index 596d015d82..ba28a77321 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp
@@ -509,9 +509,11 @@ static void BuildDirectColumnData(ClientContext &client, const vector<LogicalTyp
 	}
 }
 
+#ifdef D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
 static idx_t ExpectedChunkCount(idx_t count) {
 	return (count + STANDARD_VECTOR_SIZE - 1) / STANDARD_VECTOR_SIZE;
 }
+#endif
 
 static void PackDirectColumnData(HashedSortGroup &hash_group) {
 	lock_guard<mutex> direct_guard(hash_group.scan_lock);
